        ],
        "id": "1795861689830609075",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 11,
          "impression_count": 9674,
          "like_count": 49,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 3
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795857651592491281",
            "type": "quoted"
          }
        ],
        "text": "Glad to see scale going in this direction: Fully private LLM leaderboard.\n\nEven has the fine print 🤓: \"To ensure leaderboard integrity, we require that models can only be featured the FIRST TIME when an organization encounters the prompts.\" https://t.co/KYHIBrvAtN"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-29T16:40:05.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795857658760802514"
        ],
        "id": "1795857658760802514",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 8,
          "impression_count": 21751,
          "like_count": 128,
          "quote_count": 1,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 5
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795857656374087970",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "4/ While LMSYS and other efforts in the community are awesome, we still think there's a lot to be desired in 3rd party evaluations.\n\nOne of our design principles is to produce evals that are impossible to overfit.\n\nAs we saw with our prior GSM1k research, we think it's critical"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-29T16:40:05.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795857656374087970"
        ],
        "id": "1795857656374087970",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 22,
          "impression_count": 44179,
          "like_count": 151,
          "quote_count": 11,
          "reply_count": 9,
          "retweet_count": 7
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795857654599852392",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "3/ We eval'd many of the leading models:\n\n- GPT-4o\n- GPT-4 Turbo\n- Claude 3 Opus\n- Gemini 1.5 Pro\n- Gemini 1.5 Flash\n- Llama3\n- Mistral Large\n\nOn Coding, Math, Instruction Following, and Multilinguality (Spanish).\n\nSee leaderboard results below. https://t.co/Z3rTCCVCaP"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-29T16:40:04.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795857654599852392"
        ],
        "id": "1795857654599852392",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 2,
          "impression_count": 17516,
          "like_count": 106,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 1,
          "retweet_count": 0
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795857651592491281",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "2/ Evaluations are a critical component of the AI ecosystem.\n\nEvals are incentives for researchers, and our evaluations set the goals for how we aim to improve our models.\n\nTrusted 3rd party evals are a missing part of the whole ecosystem, which is why @scale_AI built these."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-29T16:40:04.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795857651592491281"
        ],
        "id": "1795857651592491281",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 713,
          "impression_count": 984850,
          "like_count": 1651,
          "quote_count": 86,
          "reply_count": 67,
          "retweet_count": 208
        },
        "text": "1/ We are launching SEAL Leaderboards—private, expert evaluations of leading frontier models.\n\nOur design principles:\n🔒Private + Unexploitable. No overfitting on evals!\n🎓Domain Expert Evals\n🏆Continuously Updated w/new Data and Models\n\nRead more in 🧵\n\nhttps://t.co/10nk53awrL https://t.co/MZZQX0KDc9"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "165221992",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T19:47:41.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795542479351259551"
        ],
        "id": "1795542479351259551",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 13,
          "impression_count": 115818,
          "like_count": 63,
          "quote_count": 7,
          "reply_count": 4,
          "retweet_count": 9
        },
        "text": "Scoop: Artificial intelligence firm @scale_AI  is scaling up in #SanFrancisco. The company has signed a new lease that’s more than 3x the size of its current downtown office — in a building that was abandoned by @Airbnb.\n@sfchronicle \n@alexandr_wang \n\nhttps://t.co/IBTslWSxY4"
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T22:54:37.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795589525315670325"
        ],
        "id": "1795589525315670325",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 3,
          "impression_count": 12492,
          "like_count": 48,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 1
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795589524128702601",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "8/ This too will be one of the great infrastructure projects of our time—ensuring we build the means of production of new data across the frontier to fuel AI progress."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T22:54:37.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795589524128702601"
        ],
        "id": "1795589524128702601",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 11,
          "impression_count": 6436,
          "like_count": 74,
          "quote_count": 3,
          "reply_count": 5,
          "retweet_count": 2
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795589522622992614",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "7/ On data, it's a bit more complicated.\n\nWe've exhausted most of the internet as pre-training data, and as previously mentioned, the gains are coming from post-training.\n\nThe next 4 years will need us to overcome data scarcity and build data abundance."
      },
      {
        "author_id": "615818451",
        "created_at": "2024-05-28T22:54:37.000Z",
        "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
          "1795589522622992614"
        ],
        "id": "1795589522622992614",
        "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
        "public_metrics": {
          "bookmark_count": 13,
          "impression_count": 6743,
          "like_count": 61,
          "quote_count": 0,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "retweet_count": 1
        },
        "referenced_tweets": [
          {
            "id": "1795589521159119245",
            "type": "replied_to"
          }
        ],
        "text": "6/ On compute—we have seen the astronomical investment into GPUs with NVIDIA's revenue growth. Staggering.\n\nNow the bottleneck is going to be—\n- how many more chips can we make\n- where will they go\n- where will the power come from\n- how tightly can we interconnect them https://t.co/0tZbd7u510"
      }
